 <table width="100%" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" cellpadding="5">
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20">Tours</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>All began here One Year Ago.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>On <STRONG>1/16/2004</STRONG> gossip website <A href="http://www.gawker.com" target=_blank>Gawker.com</A> reported that <STRONG>Madonna was going to tour in the summer 2004</STRONG>. <BR><A href="http://gawker.com" target=_blank>Gawker</A> wrote: </P>
<P><EM>"<STRONG>Madonna World Tour 2004</STRONG> <BR><BR>Singer. Songwriter. Producer. Actress. Author. Superstar. <BR><BR>No matter what you call her, when Madonna hits the road this Spring for her first tour since 2001’s Drowned World Tour, you can expect an evening of high energy entertainment! <BR><BR>Madonna will kick of her World Tour 2004 on June 1 in San Francisco and will continue to play arenas in <STRONG>32 US markets</STRONG>, followed by performances in <STRONG>12-15 European markets</STRONG> as well as four dates in <STRONG>Israel</STRONG>. <BR><BR>The U.S. leg of the tour goes on sale nationally on March 1."</EM> </P>
<P><IMG src="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/images/2004/tourbook/01.jpg" width=300 align=right border=0>Soon the Net and media were filled with rumors and <EM>"maybe"</EM>&nbsp;about this possible Tour <STRONG>until on February 18 2004 </STRONG><A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com"><STRONG>Drowned Madonna</STRONG></A><STRONG> discovered the calling for the dancers auditions for the upcoming world tour, giving for the first time the official confirmation to the news (<A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=1370" target=_blank>LINK</A>)</STRONG>. <STRONG>Shortly later our World Exclusive became a public issue and the day after was stated on the headlines all over the world!</STRONG></P>
<P>From that moment on, <A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com">Drowned Madonna</A> Team decided to inform the online community about every step of the creative process <STRONG>helped by&nbsp;some dancers</STRONG> that actually succeeded to be chosen by Madonna herself for the Reinvention adventure! <BR>Doing so, <STRONG>we put our credibility on a risk</STRONG> (In fact our info have been challenged for months) because when&nbsp;creating a great show like The Reinvention Tour things change pretty radically day by day until the final set, <STRONG>as Mike McKnight confirmed</STRONG> (see our interviews with <STRONG>Mike McKnight</STRONG>).&nbsp;</P>
<P>Here are some of our <STRONG>exclusive newsbits</STRONG>:</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Dancers auditions announcement</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;New York dancers auditions location (<STRONG>S.I.R. studios</STRONG>)</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>NY dancers auditions reportage</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Tour director (<STRONG>Jamie King</STRONG>)</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Dancers have been asked to dance&nbsp;combination of <STRONG>tango</STRONG> to the introduction of <STRONG>Die Another Day</STRONG> (album version)</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Dancers were taught to tango for Die Another Day from an <STRONG>Argentinean couple</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> attended the second day of the NY dancers auditions with <STRONG>Jamie King</STRONG> and <STRONG>Caresse Henry</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;We revealed the first date of the rehearsals in Los Angeles</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Dancers&nbsp;were going to do&nbsp;a <STRONG>photo shoot in&nbsp;LA</STRONG>&nbsp;<BR><BR><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>LA dancers auditions reportage</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;During the LA audition, Madonna explained the dancers that <STRONG>Die Another Day</STRONG> was going to be kind of a <STRONG>LOVE/HATE thing</STRONG>, <STRONG>very sexy, but very fighty&nbsp;between Madonna and one male dancer</STRONG>. </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;During the LA audition, Madonna was asking the dancers very unusual questions like their <STRONG>star sign</STRONG>, favourite color and stuff like that. Madonna was very funny and very kind - <EM><STRONG>One of the female dancers later revealed this info to a newspaper</STRONG></EM></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;At the LA auditions, the dancers used 6 feet long sticks and top hats for <STRONG>Hollywood</STRONG>. </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>More old&nbsp;hits&nbsp;to be performed this time</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>This time Madonna&nbsp;was going to be way more involved in the dancing routines... she was going&nbsp;full of dancing</STRONG>.&nbsp;Dancing&nbsp;was going to be&nbsp;<STRONG>hard very athletic</STRONG>. Very "<STRONG>Blond Ambition</STRONG>"... hence all the rehearsals. </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Tour book info </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Madonna&nbsp;was rehearsing with a <STRONG>guitar</STRONG> the <STRONG>Love Profusion Headcleanr Mix</STRONG> - <EM><STRONG>Mike McKnight</STRONG> talked about it later during our interviews with him.</EM></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;The tour was going to&nbsp;have <STRONG>more than one costume designer</STRONG> </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Part of the creative team of <STRONG>Cirque Du Soleil</STRONG>&nbsp;was joining the creative team for the choreography of one of the sections - <EM>See the&nbsp;<STRONG>Carnivale&nbsp;set</STRONG></EM> </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Bedtime Story</STRONG> was rehearsed by the dancers</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Madonna&nbsp;rehearsed Peter Rauhofer’s Perfect Private Life Mix of <STRONG>Nobody Knows Me</STRONG> for the show.&nbsp; </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;There was going to be a <STRONG>20’s section</STRONG> of the show with <STRONG>Hollywood</STRONG> - <EM>See the <STRONG>Carnivale set</STRONG></EM>&nbsp;</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;The show was going to&nbsp;feature <STRONG>girl on girl actions</STRONG> -&nbsp;<EM>See <STRONG>Hanky Panky</STRONG> choreography</EM></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Many wigs</STRONG> were going to&nbsp;be used&nbsp;</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Part of the show is very <STRONG>old school feel</STRONG> with&nbsp;<STRONG>Deeper and Deeper</STRONG> and <STRONG>Bad Girl</STRONG> - <EM>our dancers mistook <STRONG>Hanky Panky</STRONG> for <STRONG>Bad Girl</STRONG></EM></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Take A Bow</STRONG> was rehearsed -&nbsp;<EM>Take A Bow was not&nbsp;in the final setlist, but <STRONG>McKnight revealed&nbsp;it was&nbsp;on the first set</STRONG></EM> </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Nothing Fails</STRONG> was rehearsed</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Vogue</STRONG> was rehearsed&nbsp;</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Like A Prayer</STRONG> was rehearsed. They&nbsp;was rehearsing a more heavy version, which&nbsp;was more dancing too.&nbsp;</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Crazy For You</STRONG> was rehearsed</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>American Life</STRONG> was reheased and Madonna&nbsp;was going to rap in it </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Madonna and Jamie King still haven’t decided on the finale</STRONG>. Among the options there were <STRONG>Die Another Day</STRONG> and <STRONG>Holiday</STRONG> - <EM>Also <STRONG>Mike McKnight</STRONG>&nbsp;talked about it later during our interview with him</EM><BR><BR><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Lament</STRONG> (from Evita OST) was rehearsed</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Imagine</STRONG> was going to be the <STRONG>big surprise</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;We revealed <STRONG>The Final Setlist</STRONG>&nbsp;</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Some details on the <STRONG>stage</STRONG> and the <STRONG>dancers</STRONG>&nbsp;</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Madonna wasn’t going to tour in Germany and Italy</STRONG>, but <STRONG>more European dates</STRONG> were going to be added - <EM>See Holland and Portugal</EM> </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>No changes in the European setlist</STRONG> </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;The <STRONG>new "purple" corset</STRONG> revealed in real time live from Manchester </P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>No broadcast at VMAs</STRONG> from the <STRONG>Slane Castle</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;Real time reportage from <STRONG>Slane Castle</STRONG> sound check and concert, revealing how the stage and the costumes have been changed</P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<STRONG>Audio and video files</STRONG></P>
<P>The magic of the re-Invention Tour wasn't over on Drowned Madonna after&nbsp;the&nbsp;tour ended&nbsp;in Lisbon. In fact, we interviewed <STRONG>Stefan Smith</STRONG> (Director of the visual effect of the <STRONG>Vogue backdrop video</STRONG>), <STRONG>Mike McKnight</STRONG> (Programmer/Keyboards) and <STRONG>Lorne Cousin</STRONG> (Bag-Piper), plus in November 2004&nbsp;we brought you the first plans for the commercial release of the re-Invention Tour <STRONG>DVD</STRONG>, that according to our insiders was already&nbsp;scheduled in <STRONG>November 2005</STRONG>.</P>
<P><EM>In the process we also made some mistakes and we apologize for them.</EM></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
