 <table width="100%" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" cellpadding="5">
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=5">Movies</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>[<a href="modules.php?name=&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=3"><font class="esclusiva">Rumours</font></a>] Madonna Finally Does Candy Darling?</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>After more than ten years of waiting, it seems <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> finally will be drag -<STRONG>Candy Darling</STRONG> on the big screen.</P>
<P>According to today's edition of <STRONG><A href="http://www.thesun.co.uk/">Sun</A></STRONG></P>
<P>"<SPAN class=norm12><FONT face=Verdana><STRONG>MADONNA</STRONG> is to play a transvestite in a Hollywood film — and she has agreed to do it for free. </FONT></P>
<P>The Queen Of Pop has been chasing the role of drag queen <STRONG>CANDY DARLING</STRONG> for years but <STRONG>has just signed the deal</STRONG>."</P>
<P>Darling starred in a number of <STRONG>ANDY WARHOL</STRONG> films and provided<STRONG> LOU REED</STRONG> with the inspiration to write CANDY SAYS and <STRONG>WALK ON THE WILD SIDE</STRONG>.</P>
<P>An insider says, "Madonna has been desperate to make a film where she can earn respect for her acting abilities. She is still trying to shake off the bad publicity from the movie SWEPT AWAY. She sees this as her big chance.</P>
<P>"She has wanted to play this part for so long because she feels so strongly about the character.</P>
<P>"She said she would do anything for the part and has agreed to work for free." </P>
<P>The final talks were held <STRONG>during a fleeting visit to New York at the end of January</STRONG>. <BR><BR><STRONG>She met</STRONG> up with her close friend and unofficial movie agent <STRONG>Bryan Lourd </STRONG>to plan her next move in the movie business. <BR><BR><STRONG>She then got together with producers from the Candy project</STRONG> - which is still to be named - and agreed to star. <BR><BR>She<STRONG> also met the team producing the film version of James Ellroy's novel The Black Dahlia</STRONG>.</P>
<P align=center><IMG src="http://www.madonnavillage.it/drownedmadonna/candyd.jpg" border=0></P>
<P align=center><EM>Candy Darling</EM></P></SPAN>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
